<h2>📰 今日新聞</h2>
<div><span class="tag">World</span><span class="tag">BBC News 2026/11/24</span></div>
<div class="news-title" lang="en">Trump faces backlash after saying he 'convinced' Nvidia to reinstate CEO Jensen Huang</div>
<div class="src">出處：https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq5y1k8ez407o（Bernd Debusmann Jr、Kali Hays，BBC News）</div>
<div class="note">※ 選自 BBC 最近 24 小時新聞（可免費閱讀）：牽動全球 AI 產業、美中科技角力與美國政壇的國際大事，也是 BBC 今日最多人閱讀的新聞。</div>
<div class="ex" style="margin-top:6px"><span class="lbl">節錄</span><span class="en" lang="en">Nvidia has <b>reinstated</b> CEO Jensen Huang just days after rejecting his offer to return to the AI chipmaker - and less than two weeks after he was forced to resign over a reported affair with a suspected Chinese spy.</span><br><span class="cite">→ Nvidia 讓執行長黃仁勳復職；就在幾天前，這家 AI 晶片公司才拒絕他回鍋的提議，而距離他因被報導與一名疑似中國間諜的女性有婚外情而被迫辭職，還不到兩週。（BBC News 導言）</span></div>

<h2>① 三個重點</h2>
<ol class="points">
  <li><b>黃仁勳不到兩週就重返執行長。</b>他在 11/12 因婚外情報導辭職（其中一名女性被指與中國情報單位有關）；董事會上週二還明確表示不打算讓他回來，週一卻宣布復職，並稱已取得美國政府高層意見，確信他復職沒有國安風險。</li>
  <li><b>川普自稱「說服」董事會，股市隨之大漲。</b>川普受訪時承認，Nvidia 股價下跌「大概」影響了他出面介入；BBC 查閱財產申報，發現他多次買賣 Nvidia 股票。復職當天 Nvidia 股價漲 31%、市值增加約 1 兆美元，也終止美股一週連跌。<span class="note">（推論，非投資建議）</span></li>
  <li><b>兩黨議員一起反彈，國會將調查。</b>民主黨 Jeffries 批評此舉「無法辯護、不負責任」並承諾徹查；共和黨 Bacon、Cotton 也提出質疑。黃仁勳 12/1 將接受眾議院三個委員會閉門訪談，兩天後再到參議院銀行委員會作證。</li>
</ol>
<div class="box">
  <h3>💡 對個人有什麼影響？<span class="note" style="font-weight:normal">（以下為整理者的分析，非新聞原文）</span></h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>投資與市場：</b>一則人事消息就讓單一公司市值一天變動上兆美元，持有科技股、AI 或半導體相關基金的人，短期內可能面對較大波動。<span class="note">（推論，非投資建議）</span></li>
    <li><b>科技與工作：</b>多位議員要求立法加強晶片出口管制；若通過，AI 晶片供應與價格可能受影響，在歐美科技業或供應鏈工作的人也可能感受到變化。</li>
    <li><b>讀新聞的眼光：</b>政治人物介入企業決策、本身又持有該公司股票時，可以多留意「利益衝突」與「誰因此得利」。</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h2>② 今日單字（5 個）</h2>
<div class="vocab">
  <div class="vhead"><span class="vnum">1</span><span class="vword" lang="en">reinstate</span><span class="vread">[͵riɪnˋstet]</span><span class="vpos">動</span><span class="vmean">使復職；恢復（資格、制度）</span></div>
  <div class="ex"><span class="lbl">例句</span><span class="en" lang="en">In July, the International Olympic Committee (IOC) provisionally <b>reinstated</b> Russia to its competitions, stating a ban introduced in 2023 after the invasion of Ukraine was "no longer applicable".</span><br><span class="cite">— BBC Sport（2026/11/13） https://www.bbc.com/sport/articles/cm4gn9lvlgy2o</span></div>
  <div class="conn"><span class="lbl">接續</span><b lang="en">reinstate＋人＋as／to＋職位</b>：常用被動 <i>be reinstated as CEO</i>；名詞 <i>reinstatement</i>。</div>
</div>
<div class="vocab">
  <div class="vhead"><span class="vnum">2</span><span class="vword" lang="en">backlash</span><span class="vread">[ˋbæk͵læʃ]</span><span class="vpos">名</span><span class="vmean">（對某事的）強烈反彈、反感</span></div>
  <div class="ex"><span class="lbl">例句</span><span class="en" lang="en">The moves come amid a mounting <b>backlash</b> over the reinstatement of athletes from Russia and Belarus.</span><br><span class="cite">— BBC Sport（2026/11/13） https://www.bbc.com/sport/articles/cm4gn9lvlgy2o</span></div>
  <div class="conn"><span class="lbl">接續</span><b lang="en">face／prompt＋backlash＋over</b>：<i>face</i>（遭受）、<i>prompt</i>（引發）；原因用 <i>over</i>。</div>
</div>
<div class="vocab">
  <div class="vhead"><span class="vnum">3</span><span class="vword" lang="en">bipartisan</span><span class="vread">[baɪˋpɑrtəzn̩]</span><span class="vpos">形</span><span class="vmean">兩黨（共同）的、跨黨派的</span></div>
  <div class="ex"><span class="lbl">例句</span><span class="en" lang="en">Even before the midterms, Congress saw <b>bipartisan</b> efforts to limit Trump's ability to continue the war with Iran.</span><br><span class="cite">— BBC News（2026/11/04） https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq1kdgnn2xdeo</span></div>
  <div class="conn"><span class="lbl">接續</span><b lang="en">bipartisan＋support／efforts／backlash</b>：放在名詞前；<i>garner bipartisan support</i>（獲兩黨支持）。</div>
</div>
<div class="vocab">
  <div class="vhead"><span class="vnum">4</span><span class="vword" lang="en">testify</span><span class="vread">[ˋtɛstə͵faɪ]</span><span class="vpos">動</span><span class="vmean">（在國會、法庭）作證</span></div>
  <div class="ex"><span class="lbl">例句</span><span class="en" lang="en">Control of the House and Senate gives the party power to issue subpoenas - summons to <b>testify</b> or produce documents - as well as additional funding to launch investigations early next year.</span><br><span class="cite">— BBC News（2026/11/05） https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvglwg033027o</span></div>
  <div class="conn"><span class="lbl">接續</span><b lang="en">testify＋before＋機關／against＋人</b>：<i>testify before Congress</i>；名詞 <i>testimony</i>（證詞）。</div>
</div>
<div class="vocab">
  <div class="vhead"><span class="vnum">5</span><span class="vword" lang="en">vow</span><span class="vread">[vaʊ]</span><span class="vpos">動</span><span class="vmean">發誓、誓言要（做某事）</span></div>
  <div class="ex"><span class="lbl">例句</span><span class="en" lang="en">Democratic lawmakers have <b>vowed</b> to look into Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's handling of the war with Iran that began in February - …</span><br><span class="cite">— BBC News（2026/11/05） https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvglwg033027o</span></div>
  <div class="conn"><span class="lbl">接續</span><b lang="en">vow＋to＋原形動詞／that 子句</b>：最常見 <i>vow to investigate</i>；名詞 <i>a vow</i>（誓言）。</div>
</div>

<h2>③ 今日重點文法</h2>
<div class="grammar">
  <div class="gtitle" lang="en">be due to ＋ 原形動詞</div>
  <div>「預定要……、照計畫將會……」：表示已排定、預期會發生的事。</div>
  <div class="formula" lang="en">主詞 ＋ be ＋ due to ＋ 原形動詞（＋時間）</div>
  <div class="ex" style="margin-top:6px"><span class="lbl">本文</span><span class="en" lang="en">But now both Trump and Nvidia are facing bipartisan backlash from lawmakers, just as Huang <b>is due to testify</b> before Congress next week.</span><br><span class="cite">→ 但現在川普和 Nvidia 都面臨兩黨議員的反彈，而黃仁勳下週就要到國會作證。（BBC 記者）</span></div>
  <table class="g">
    <tr><th>用法</th><td>表示「預定、排定」，常見於行程、會議、出庭、發布等；語氣比 <i lang="en">will</i> 更正式。</td></tr>
    <tr><th>前接</th><td><i lang="en">be</i> 動詞隨主詞與時態變化：<i lang="en">is／are／was due to</i>；<i lang="en">was due to</i> 常暗示「原本預定，但沒發生」。</td></tr>
    <tr><th>易混淆用法</th><td><i lang="en">be due to＋原形動詞</i>（預定要做） vs. <i lang="en">due to＋名詞</i>（因為……），如 <i lang="en">due to the strike</i>。</td></tr>
    <tr><th>後接</th><td>原形動詞，常再加時間：<i lang="en">due to testify next week</i>、<i lang="en">due to stage … in March</i>。</td></tr>
    <tr><th>注意</th><td>接動詞時一定用原形；只講時間可用 <i lang="en">be due＋時間</i>（如報告、帳單的到期日）。</td></tr>
  </table>
  <div class="ex"><span class="lbl">例句</span><span class="en" lang="en">Norway is preparing to host the cross-country skiing World Cup next month, while Finland <b>is due to stage</b> the figure skating world championships in March.</span><br>
  <span class="cite">— BBC Sport（2026/11/13） https://www.bbc.com/sport/articles/cm4gn9lvlgy2o</span></div>
</div>

